Z||000000||Cliff D.||06-03-2001||08:59 PM||||I cannot find this simple answer anywhere in my factory service manual. Can someone please explain to me how the cylinders on the 2.8 are numbered. Is it (left to right) 1,3,5 behind the driver and 2,4,6 at the back of the car?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||06-03-2001||09:05 PM||||stand on the pass side of your fiero and look at the engine (this is the frt with the belts), you will see that one side of engine the valve cover is closer to you than the other.  The closest to you is number 1. Number two is on the other side.  so 1 3 5 on one side and 2 4 6 on the other.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff D.||06-03-2001||09:18 PM||||Thanks, looks like I was exactly 180 degrees off.||||reg||1
